For performance optimization, consider using non-blocking UUID generation when possible and limiting the precision of the timestamp to reduce filename length. Additionally, you should handle potential errors gracefully and provide logging for tracking the generation process.

Lastly, integrate with your external configuration management system for versioning and logging by replacing `get_version()` and `update_version()` functions, as well as the `log_event()` function. This will help you maintain and extend this utility in a larger system undergoing continuous integration and deployment processes.']

